  "selected_statement": {
    "theorem": "5.20-generic-quantum-Harish-Chandra",
    "doi": "10.5802/jep.326"
  },
  "closure": "Exact entire mathematical body116–2572 and original preamble6–78 retained with matching official bibliography. Original Theorem5.20 statement2349–2351 and full primary2353–2357 are accompanied by the exact generic base field1966–1970, all quantum Hamiltonian reduction/source ring/invariant quotient definitions2210–2263, explicit coefficient ring2185 and all four generic generator-image formulas2341–2344. Literal self-reference2239, exponent2244 and rad_k summary2336 remain unchanged and visibly flagged; no new definition/moment calculation supplied. Entire new quantum-trace/invariant/classical degeneration1599–1964 and filtered localization/generation/PBW/invariant comparison support retained. Complete generic Etingof–Kirillov/Verma model1966–2046, diagrammatic admissibility/partial adjoints/product/action2047–2208, full moment reduction2210–2234, generator/Nakayama2262 and Pieri/specialization2265–2325 retained. Exact original ribbon-isotopy prerequisite812–816 (Reshetikhin–Turaev) and all drawn braid/duality/product conventions included; drawing exercise2131 is the bounded associativity check for the already-drawn product/action, not an editor-generated construction. Unproved whole-space action2195 is retained as unselected remark; full restricted tHom_D/Int action2189–2208 used. Exact common k>2n generator condition and arbitrarily-large-k compatibility2311–2324 retained, without selecting separate all-k>n strengthening. Published Cherednik faithful polynomial representation, Etingof–Kirillov Macdonald theory, Jordan PBW/moment maps, Gan–Ginzburg almost commuting invariants and BGG tensor-Verma decomposition remain precisely attributed prerequisites. Forty unique necessary original diagram assets (41 occurrences) are exact embedded PDF Form streams with recursive resources, including every full action/product/moment diagram; all surrounding statement/proof text/formulas remain editable. bbm uses only32 exact source-observed digit1 calls with source-specific one-dimensional representation/unit semantics, rendered in pinned installed Noto U+1D7D9 with mathord/source-size adaptation and unknown-argument rejection. No mathematical proof generation, source correction or independent refereeing.",
  "current_difficulty_reason": "The published ribbon-category, Macdonald and PBW prerequisites do not themselves construct the generic radial-parts action because the required Verma modules have no coevaluation. The author supplies new admissible-diagram and restricted-action constructions, verifies the full quantum moment reduction, and proves Pieri preservation and compatibility at infinitely many integral specializations. The remaining generic isomorphism then uses the fully retained local invariant/classical-degeneration dimension and finite-generation/localization arguments, rather than being a formal relabeling of the finite-dimensional theorem.",
  "editorial_changes": [
    "Independent article layout and explicit source, scope and difficulty boundary",
    "Bibliography restored from exact matching cached publisher HTML with native math annotations",
    "Necessary native macro definitions retained; only publisher typography commands mapped to ordinary article equivalents",
    "Recover original embedded PDF Form diagrams byte exact with recursive resources; wrapper-only graphicspath with trailing slash, no author-body modification."
